{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "H^*(RP^4; Z)\n  H^0 = Z\n  H^1 = 0\n  H^2 = Z/2\n  H^3 = 0\n  H^4 = Z/2\n  universal coefficients: H^n(X; G) = Hom(H_n X, G) + Ext(H_{n-1} X, G) for n = 0..4\n  check: d o d = 0 (6), universal coefficients (5)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "cohomology", "ucas": "cohomology RP^4", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "cohomology", "space": "RP^4", "coefficients": "Z", "groups": [{"degree": 0, "group": "Z", "rank": 1, "torsion": []}, {"degree": 1, "group": "0", "rank": 0, "torsion": []}, {"degree": 2, "group": "Z/2", "rank": 0, "torsion": ["2"]}, {"degree": 3, "group": "0", "rank": 0, "torsion": []}, {"degree": 4, "group": "Z/2", "rank": 0, "torsion": ["2"]}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "d o d = 0", "points": 6, "passed": true, "text": "d o d = 0: verified 6 times"}, {"kind": "universal coefficients", "points": 5, "passed": true, "text": "universal coefficients: verified 5 times"}], "files": [], "text": "H^*(RP^4; Z)\n  H^0 = Z\n  H^1 = 0\n  H^2 = Z/2\n  H^3 = 0\n  H^4 = Z/2\n  universal coefficients: H^n(X; G) = Hom(H_n X, G) + Ext(H_{n-1} X, G) for n = 0..4\n  check: d o d = 0 (6), universal coefficients (5)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Bockstein spectral sequence of L(9,1) at p = 3\n  (the exact couple of 0 -> C -3-> C -> C (x) Z/3 -> 0: D_1 = H^*(L(9,1); Z), E_1 = H^*(L(9,1); Z/3), i = 3, j = reduction, k = Bockstein)\n  D_1 = Z, 0, Z/9, Z   (degrees 0..3)\n  E_1 = Z/3, Z/3, Z/3, Z/3   (degrees 0..3)\n  d_1: 0\n  D_2 = Z, 0, Z/3, Z   (degrees 0..3)\n  E_2 = Z/3, Z/3, Z/3, Z/3   (degrees 0..3)\n  d_2: E^1 -> E^2 [[1]]\n  D_3 = Z, 0, 0, Z   (degrees 0..3)\n  E_3 = Z/3, 0, 0, Z/3   (degrees 0..3)\n  d_3: 0\n  stable from page 3: i_3 is injective in every degree, so k_3 = 0, d_r = 0 and E_r = E_3 for every r >= 3 (E_inf = E_3)\n  (d_r in the canonical generators of E_r^n; every page derived exactly: D' = i D, E' = ker d / im d, i' j' k' checked well defined, each couple checked exact)\n  check: d o d = 0 (28), d maps relations to relations (3), chain map commutes with d (8), induced map well defined (48), exact (60), short exact (degree) (4), snake lemma lift (3), stable page: d = 0, next page equal (4)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "bockstein", "ucas": "bockstein L(9) mod 3", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "bockstein", "space": "L(9,1)", "p": 3, "pages": [{"page": 1, "D": ["Z", "0", "Z/9", "Z"], "E": ["Z/3", "Z/3", "Z/3", "Z/3"], "d": []}, {"page": 2, "D": ["Z", "0", "Z/3", "Z"], "E": ["Z/3", "Z/3", "Z/3", "Z/3"], "d": [{"from": 1, "to": 2, "matrix": "[[1]]"}]}, {"page": 3, "D": ["Z", "0", "0", "Z"], "E": ["Z/3", "0", "0", "Z/3"], "d": []}], "stable_page": 3, "E_inf": ["Z/3", "0", "0", "Z/3"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "d o d = 0", "points": 28, "passed": true, "text": "d o d = 0: verified 28 times"}, {"kind": "d maps relations to relations", "points": 3, "passed": true, "text": "d maps relations to relations: verified 3 times"}, {"kind": "chain map commutes with d", "points": 8, "passed": true, "text": "chain map commutes with d: verified 8 times"}, {"kind": "induced map well defined", "points": 48, "passed": true, "text": "induced map well defined: verified 48 times"}, {"kind": "exact", "points": 60, "passed": true, "text": "exact: verified 60 times"}, {"kind": "short exact (degree)", "points": 4, "passed": true, "text": "short exact (degree): verified 4 times"}, {"kind": "snake lemma lift", "points": 3, "passed": true, "text": "snake lemma lift: verified 3 times"}, {"kind": "stable page: d = 0, next page equal", "points": 4, "passed": true, "text": "stable page: d = 0, next page equal: verified 4 times"}], "files": [], "text": "Bockstein spectral sequence of L(9,1) at p = 3\n  (the exact couple of 0 -> C -3-> C -> C (x) Z/3 -> 0: D_1 = H^*(L(9,1); Z), E_1 = H^*(L(9,1); Z/3), i = 3, j = reduction, k = Bockstein)\n  D_1 = Z, 0, Z/9, Z   (degrees 0..3)\n  E_1 = Z/3, Z/3, Z/3, Z/3   (degrees 0..3)\n  d_1: 0\n  D_2 = Z, 0, Z/3, Z   (degrees 0..3)\n  E_2 = Z/3, Z/3, Z/3, Z/3   (degrees 0..3)\n  d_2: E^1 -> E^2 [[1]]\n  D_3 = Z, 0, 0, Z   (degrees 0..3)\n  E_3 = Z/3, 0, 0, Z/3   (degrees 0..3)\n  d_3: 0\n  stable from page 3: i_3 is injective in every degree, so k_3 = 0, d_r = 0 and E_r = E_3 for every r >= 3 (E_inf = E_3)\n  (d_r in the canonical generators of E_r^n; every page derived exactly: D' = i D, E' = ker d / im d, i' j' k' checked well defined, each couple checked exact)\n  check: d o d = 0 (28), d maps relations to relations (3), chain map commutes with d (8), induced map well defined (48), exact (60), short exact (degree) (4), snake lemma lift (3), stable page: d = 0, next page equal (4)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Proposition 0.1 on S^2 x RP^3 at p = 2: if a in H^n(X; Z) generates a Z summand, then abar = j_r(p^(r-1) a) is in ker d_r^n and not in im d_r^(n-1), for every r >= 1\n  stable from page 2: i_2 is injective in every degree, so k_2 = 0, d_r = 0 and E_r = E_2 for every r >= 2 (E_inf = E_2)\n  n = 0: H^0 = Z\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^0 [ok]; ker(H^0 -> E_1^0 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^0 [ok]; ker(H^0 -> E_2^0 / im d_2) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n  n = 1: H^1 = 0 (no Z summand: nothing to prove; checked anyway)\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^1 [ok]; ker(H^1 -> E_1^1 / im d_1) has content 0 [vacuous]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^1 [ok]; ker(H^1 -> E_2^1 / im d_2) has content 0 [vacuous]\n  n = 2: H^2 = Z/2 + Z\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^2 [ok]; ker(H^2 -> E_1^2 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^2 [ok]; ker(H^2 -> E_2^2 / im d_2) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n  n = 3: H^3 = Z\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^3 [ok]; ker(H^3 -> E_1^3 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^3 [ok]; ker(H^3 -> E_2^3 / im d_2) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n  n = 4: H^4 = Z/2 (no Z summand: nothing to prove; checked anyway)\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^4 [ok]; ker(H^4 -> E_1^4 / im d_1) has content 0 [vacuous]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^4 [ok]; ker(H^4 -> E_2^4 / im d_2) has content 0 [vacuous]\n  n = 5: H^5 = Z\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^5 [ok]; ker(H^5 -> E_1^5 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^5 [ok]; ker(H^5 -> E_2^5 / im d_2) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n  why this is complete: a generates a Z summand of H iff its class in H/T(H) is primitive; psi_r(a) = [j_r(p^(r-1) a)] in E_r^n / im d_r^(n-1) vanishes iff a is in K = ker psi_r, and the image of K in the free group H/T(H) contains a primitive vector iff the gcd of its coordinates (the content) is 1\n  r > 2: page 2 is stable (i_2 injective: k = 0, and i_2 is an isomorphism of exact couples onto page 3 with j_(r+1)(p^r a) = j_r(p^(r-1) a)), so every later page and every abar is the one at r = 2\n  holds for every n and every r >= 1\n  check: d o d = 0 (35), d maps relations to relations (5), chain map commutes with d (12), induced map well defined (67), exact (72), short exact (degree) (6), snake lemma lift (7), stable page: d = 0, next page equal (6)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "prop01", "ucas": "prop01 S^2 x RP^3 mod 2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "prop01", "space": "S^2 x RP^3", "p": 2, "stable_page": 2, "degrees": [{"degree": 0, "H": "Z", "pages": [{"page": 1, "in_ker": true, "content": "2", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}, {"page": 2, "in_ker": true, "content": "2", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}]}, {"degree": 1, "H": "0", "pages": [{"page": 1, "in_ker": true, "content": "0", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}, {"page": 2, "in_ker": true, "content": "0", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}]}, {"degree": 2, "H": "Z/2 + Z", "pages": [{"page": 1, "in_ker": true, "content": "2", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}, {"page": 2, "in_ker": true, "content": "2", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}]}, {"degree": 3, "H": "Z", "pages": [{"page": 1, "in_ker": true, "content": "2", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}, {"page": 2, "in_ker": true, "content": "2", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}]}, {"degree": 4, "H": "Z/2", "pages": [{"page": 1, "in_ker": true, "content": "0", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}, {"page": 2, "in_ker": true, "content": "0", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}]}, {"degree": 5, "H": "Z", "pages": [{"page": 1, "in_ker": true, "content": "2", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}, {"page": 2, "in_ker": true, "content": "2", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}]}], "holds": true}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "d o d = 0", "points": 35, "passed": true, "text": "d o d = 0: verified 35 times"}, {"kind": "d maps relations to relations", "points": 5, "passed": true, "text": "d maps relations to relations: verified 5 times"}, {"kind": "chain map commutes with d", "points": 12, "passed": true, "text": "chain map commutes with d: verified 12 times"}, {"kind": "induced map well defined", "points": 67, "passed": true, "text": "induced map well defined: verified 67 times"}, {"kind": "exact", "points": 72, "passed": true, "text": "exact: verified 72 times"}, {"kind": "short exact (degree)", "points": 6, "passed": true, "text": "short exact (degree): verified 6 times"}, {"kind": "snake lemma lift", "points": 7, "passed": true, "text": "snake lemma lift: verified 7 times"}, {"kind": "stable page: d = 0, next page equal", "points": 6, "passed": true, "text": "stable page: d = 0, next page equal: verified 6 times"}], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "checked for every degree and every page up to the stable one; later pages are isomorphic to it"}, "files": [], "text": "Proposition 0.1 on S^2 x RP^3 at p = 2: if a in H^n(X; Z) generates a Z summand, then abar = j_r(p^(r-1) a) is in ker d_r^n and not in im d_r^(n-1), for every r >= 1\n  stable from page 2: i_2 is injective in every degree, so k_2 = 0, d_r = 0 and E_r = E_2 for every r >= 2 (E_inf = E_2)\n  n = 0: H^0 = Z\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^0 [ok]; ker(H^0 -> E_1^0 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^0 [ok]; ker(H^0 -> E_2^0 / im d_2) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n  n = 1: H^1 = 0 (no Z summand: nothing to prove; checked anyway)\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^1 [ok]; ker(H^1 -> E_1^1 / im d_1) has content 0 [vacuous]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^1 [ok]; ker(H^1 -> E_2^1 / im d_2) has content 0 [vacuous]\n  n = 2: H^2 = Z/2 + Z\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^2 [ok]; ker(H^2 -> E_1^2 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^2 [ok]; ker(H^2 -> E_2^2 / im d_2) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n  n = 3: H^3 = Z\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^3 [ok]; ker(H^3 -> E_1^3 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^3 [ok]; ker(H^3 -> E_2^3 / im d_2) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n  n = 4: H^4 = Z/2 (no Z summand: nothing to prove; checked anyway)\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^4 [ok]; ker(H^4 -> E_1^4 / im d_1) has content 0 [vacuous]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^4 [ok]; ker(H^4 -> E_2^4 / im d_2) has content 0 [vacuous]\n  n = 5: H^5 = Z\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^5 [ok]; ker(H^5 -> E_1^5 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^5 [ok]; ker(H^5 -> E_2^5 / im d_2) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n  why this is complete: a generates a Z summand of H iff its class in H/T(H) is primitive; psi_r(a) = [j_r(p^(r-1) a)] in E_r^n / im d_r^(n-1) vanishes iff a is in K = ker psi_r, and the image of K in the free group H/T(H) contains a primitive vector iff the gcd of its coordinates (the content) is 1\n  r > 2: page 2 is stable (i_2 injective: k = 0, and i_2 is an isomorphism of exact couples onto page 3 with j_(r+1)(p^r a) = j_r(p^(r-1) a)), so every later page and every abar is the one at r = 2\n  holds for every n and every r >= 1\n  check: d o d = 0 (35), d maps relations to relations (5), chain map commutes with d (12), induced map well defined (67), exact (72), short exact (degree) (6), snake lemma lift (7), stable page: d = 0, next page equal (6)\n"}, "isError": false}}
